essure during pregnancy with increased bone lead levels</article-title><source>Am J Epidemiol</source><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12480651</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B5"><label>5</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Glenn</surname><given-names>BS</given-names></name><name><surname>Stewart</surname><given-names>WF</given-names></name><name><surname>Links</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Todd</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name><name><surname>Schwartz</surname><given-names>BS</given-names></name></person-group><volume>14</volume><issue>1</issue><year>2003</year><fpage>30</fpage><lpage>36</lpage><article-title>The longitudinal association of&#x000a0;lead with blood pressure</article-title><source>Epidemiology</source><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12500043</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><label>6</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gerr</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Letz</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Stokes</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Chettle</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>McNeill</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Kaye</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><volume>42</volume><issue>2</issue><year>2002</year><fpage>98</fpage><lpage>106</lpage><article-title>Association between bone lead&#x000a0;concentration and blood pressure among young adults</article-title><source>Am J Ind Med</source><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12125085</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><label>7</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Roper</surname><given-names>WL</given-names></name><name><surname>Houk</surname><given-names>VN</given-names></name><name><surname>Falk</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><su